pip install fastapi uvicorn
2. Basic FastAPI initialization
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI(
    title="Gemini API Service",
    description="FastAPI service for Gemini API integration",
    version="1.0.0"
)

@app.get("/")
async def root():
    return {"message": "FastAPI is running"}

@app.get("/health")
async def health():
    return {"status": "healthy"}
3. Run the API
uvicorn main:app --reload

Then open:

http://127.0.0.1:8000

Interactive API documentation:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
4. If you're connecting Gemini
pip install fastapi uvicorn google-genai python-dotenv
import os

from fastapi import FastAPI
from google import genai
from dotenv import load_dotenv

load_dotenv()

app = FastAPI(title="Gemini FastAPI")

client = genai.Client(
    api_key=os.getenv("GEMINI_API_KEY")
)

@app.get("/health")
async def health():
    return {"status": "ok", "gemini": "configured"}

A typical project structure is:

project/
├── main.py
├── .env
└── requirements.txt

.env:

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

requirements.txt:

fastapi
uvicorn[standard]
google-genai
python-dotenv

Do not put the Gemini API key directly in your Python source code.
